WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.630
A boy in my class once told a

2
00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:05.110
game's chat robot his full name,

3
00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:07.410
his school and where he lives.

4
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:09.640
It asked him so nicely!

5
00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.900
But where did those secrets go?

6
00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:17.350
Today: what you never tell a chatbot, and

7
00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.950
why an AI can repeat what it's told.

8
00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.790
When you type into a chatbot, your words

9
00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.450
travel to a big computer far away.

10
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.460
They can be saved there.

11
00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:30.250
People who work for the

12
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.490
app might read them.

13
00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:34.210
And some apps use them to teach their AI.

14
00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:36.400
And here's a surprise.

15
00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:39.100
An AI can remember things it learned,

16
00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.180
and say them again to someone else.

17
00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:44.570
A secret you tell it might come out later.

18
00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:47.540
So some things are secrets.

19
00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:51.730
Your full name, your address, your

20
00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:53.770
school and your phone number.

21
00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:55.180
Your passwords.

22
00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:58.370
And photos of you or your family.

23
00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:00.040
Quick check!

24
00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:03.540
A friendly chatbot in a game asks: “What's

25
00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:05.460
your address, so I can send you a prize?”

26
00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:06.910
What do you do?

27
00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:10.570
Don't tell it, and ask a grown-up.

28
00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:13.050
A prize is a common trick

29
00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:13.850
to get your secrets.

30
00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.720
Even part of your address is too much.

31
00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:19.970
Some toys and speakers can

32
00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:21.230
talk and listen too.

33
00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:23.380
They can send what you say to

34
00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:24.560
a computer far away.

35
00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:27.620
Treat them like a chatbot: no secrets.

36
00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.900
Before you use a new AI app, ask a

37
00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:33.360
grown-up at home or at school.

38
00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:35.630
Many apps are not made for

39
00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:36.550
children your age.

40
00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.620
A grown-up can help you choose a safe one.

41
00:01:40.690 --> 00:01:44.270
In the app, a tiny AI learned one made-up

42
00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.590
secret: Ms Amina's library card number!

43
00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:49.670
Ask it to finish the secret

44
00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:51.630
line, and it says the number.

45
00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:53.970
Add privacy, and the

46
00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:55.510
secret stops coming out.

47
00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:57.360
Your turn.

48
00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:00.690
You want a chatbot to help with a

49
00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:02.270
story about your best friend.

50
00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:03.890
What do you type?

51
00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:07.610
The made-up story is best: no

52
00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:09.150
real names, no photos.

53
00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:12.230
Remember: your words travel,

54
00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:14.710
and an AI can repeat them.

55
00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:16.860
Keep your secrets out.

56
00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:19.280
And ask a grown-up before

57
00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:20.500
you use a new app.

58
00:02:21.710 --> 00:02:24.890
Try it tomorrow: make a “Secret or OK?”

59
00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:27.120
list with a grown-up at home.

60
00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:29.770
Write things you might type into an app.

61
00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:33.690
Mark each one: secret, or OK to share.
